```

However, if you want to change the color of the joke text only, you can use a CSS pseudo-element to target the text content of the `#joke-container` element.

**Updated CSS (style.css)**

```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    text-align: center;
}

#joke-container {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: 18px;
}

#joke-container::before {
    content: "Joke: ";
    color: red;
}

#joke-container::after {
    content: "\nAuthor: ";
    color: red;
}
```

In this updated CSS, we're using the `::before` and `::after` pseudo-elements to target the text content of the `#joke-container` element. We're setting the color of these pseudo-elements to red, which will change the color of the joke text.

